\f1\fs22 The chair had a commanding view of the rainforest, which Johnny regarded as one of its defects. An Airborne should never be this close to the ground, even beyond the reach of the Layer.\
A king parrot landed on the glass in front of him.\
Johnny regarded it.\
The parrot turned around and shat down the window.\
\'93Tax.\'94\
Chip came in.\
He looked at the window, then at Johnny sitting in Sarah\'92s chair.\
Johnny settled further into it.\
Dr Quark was already at the far end of the table, reading from his device. He acknowledged nobody.\
Eloise entered last.\
\'93Sarah is on stress leave,\'94 Johnny announced.\
\'93I know where Sarah is.\'94\
Johnny nodded as though he had provided useful confirmation.\
Eloise sat.\
Chip remained standing.\
\'93Dr Quark,\'94 Eloise said. \'93You\'92ve reviewed everything Mr Stockwell has provided?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93And?\'94\
\'93My assessment hasn\'92t changed.\'94\
Chip drew breath.\
Eloise raised one finger. \'93We have already had that meeting.\'94\
Chip shut his mouth.\
Johnny failed to hide his satisfaction.\
\'93So,\'94 he said.\
Eloise looked at him.\
Johnny reconsidered whatever had been coming next.\
Eloise turned to Chip. \'93Are you going to continue obstructing Project Kebab?\'94\
\'93I\'92m going to continue telling you when you\'92re doing something dangerous.\'94\
\'93That wasn\'92t my question.\'94\
\'93It\'92s the answer you\'92re getting.\'94\
Johnny rolled his eyes.\
Chip saw him.\
The eye-rolling stopped.\
Quark continued reading.\
Eloise rested her hands on the table. \'93You were employed because you knew things we did not.\'94\
\'93I still do.\'94\
\'93That has become difficult to distinguish from you merely saying you know things we do not.\'94\
Chip looked towards Quark.\
Quark turned a page on his device.\
\'93You know why I can\'92t give you the evidence,\'94 Chip said.\
\'93I know why you say you can\'92t,\'94 Quark answered.\
Johnny smiled.\
Chip slowly turned towards him.\
Johnny\'92s smile became something he needed to do with his mouth while looking elsewhere.\
\'93I warned you about five discs,\'94 Chip said.\
\'93We are not doing this again,\'94 Eloise said.\
\'93I warned you about coherence.\'94\
\'93Mr Stockwell.\'94\
\'93I warned you\'97\'94\
\'93I heard you the first time.\'94\
The room fell quiet.\
Outside, the parrot climbed sideways across the glass to inspect its work.\
Johnny glanced at it and moved his chair a little.\
Chip planted both hands on the table.\
\'93You keep going, I keep getting in the way.\'94\
Eloise considered him.\
\'93That, at least, is clear.\'94\
Johnny sat forward. \'93Exactly.\'94\
Eloise didn\'92t look at him. \'93Be quiet.\'94\
He sat back.\
Chip\'92s hands stayed on the table.\
\'93You have another problem,\'94 Eloise said.\
\'93I\'92ve got several.\'94\
\'93You removed confidential Fridge Force material and supplied it to Sarah.\'94\
Chip\'92s face changed by almost nothing.\
\'93I gave her information she needed.\'94\
\'93That is the sort of distinction people make after they have stolen something.\'94\
\'93Corporate secrets don\'92t trump planetary safety.\'94\
\'93No. But corporate espionage remains corporate espionage.\'94\
Chip straightened.\
Johnny looked pleased again.\
Eloise continued. \'93There is also the question of whether your relationship with Fridge Force actually ended when you came here.\'94\
Johnny\'92s pleasure became fascination.\
Chip stared at Eloise.\
\'93You know it did.\'94\
\'93I know you say it did.\'94\
\'93You\'92re calling me a spy?\'94\
\'93I\'92m saying I have a security problem.\'94\
\'93I\'92m your security problem because I won\'92t let Stoat turn the washing machine back on?\'94\
Johnny bristled. \'93You don\'92t let me do anything.\'94\
\'93That may be the first accurate thing you\'92ve said today,\'94 Chip told him.\
Johnny started to rise.\
Chip looked at him.\
Johnny sat.\
Quark removed his glasses and cleaned them.\
Eloise watched Chip for a moment.\
\'93When you joined this project, your objections were useful.\'94\
\'93They still are.\'94\
\'93No. They are now preventing progress.\'94\
\'93That\'92s the idea.\'94\
Eloise smiled faintly.\
Chip realised too late that he had helped her.\
She lifted her device.\
Two security officers appeared at the double doors.\
Johnny looked quickly from them to Chip and rolled Sarah\'92s chair backwards until the table was between them.\
Chip ignored him.\
\'93You\'92re serious,\'94 he said.\
\'93I generally am by the time security arrives.\'94\
\'93You put me in a cell, you lose the only person here who knows what this thing can do.\'94\
Dr Quark looked up.\
Eloise did too.\
For a second Chip seemed to regret the sentence.\
Then it was gone.\
Eloise spoke to the officers.\
\'93Take Mr Stockwell downstairs.\'94\
One of them glanced at Chip\'92s dimensions and then at his colleague.\
\'93Where, ma\'92am?\'94\
\'93The brig.\'94\
Chip laughed once.\
Not because anything was funny.\
He pushed his chair under the table.\
Johnny watched him come around it and rolled himself another metre away.\
Chip stopped beside Sarah\'92s chair.\
\'93Keep it warm, Stoat.\'94\
Johnny said nothing.\
Chip walked out between the security officers.\
The king parrot tapped on the glass.\
Eloise looked at Johnny.\
\'93Move out of Sarah\'92s chair.\'94\

